<title>FRANCE: French crude imports fell in March.</title>
<headline>French crude imports fell in March.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's industry ministry issued the following data for deliveries to refineries, margins and capacity utilisation. Crude deliveries by origin ('000 tonnes).</p>
<p>					    Mar 1997   Feb 1997 Mar 1996</p>
<p>    Total				 6,654	7,032    7,449</p>
<p>    Middle East			 2,009	2,806    2,631</p>
<p>    including Saudi Arabia	    774	1,385    1,312</p>
<p>		  Iraq			425	  599	  0</p>
<p>		  Iran			453	  469    1,077</p>
<p>		  Kuwait			7	  272	  0</p>
<p>    Africa				1,410	  904    1,580</p>
<p>    including Algeria		   398	  482	368</p>
<p>		  Libya		     162	   79	209</p>
<p>		  Nigeria		   653	  316	864</p>
<p>    OECD Europe			 2,546	2,523    2,332</p>
<p>    including Britain		 1,109	  945    1,149</p>
<p>		  Norway		  1,239	1,439    1,001</p>
<p>		  France		    146	  139	182</p>
<p>    Other				   688	  799	906</p>
<p>    including Venezuela		   0	    0	  0</p>
<p>		  Mexico			0	    0	  0</p>
<p>		  ex-USSR		   688	  799	906</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following data for French refining margins, based on North Sea Brent crude ($/barrel).</p>
<p>			    Apr 1997  Mar 1997  Feb 1997  Apr 1996</p>
<p>    Refining Margin     3.31	2.62	1.59	1.86</p>
<p>In the most recent month for which refinery capacity utilisation is available, French plants ran at 75 percent of capacity in March, when several units had spring maintenance.</p>
<p>The figure is down from 89 percent in February and 96 percent in January.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
